<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria 56-day T-bills sold out, yielding 290 pct.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria 56-day T-bills sold out, yielding 290 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry issue of 3.0 billion levs of one-year discount T-bills was sold out, yielding record high 289.54 percent, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The central bank and four other financial instituitions took part in Monday's auction, the BNB said in a statement.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		BG 3018096001</p>
<p> Type			  Discount</p>
<p> Par value		   3.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date		Sept 16, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date		  Sept 18, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	     Nov 13, 1996</p>
<p> Bids received	     3.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	 81.17 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved	     3.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	81.17 pct</p>
<p> Yield to maturity	 23.20 pct</p>
<p> Cumulative annual yield 289.54 pct -- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
</text>
